  "title": "The Plant That Leaned Toward Two Desks",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "silent emotional stories",
  "premise": "Two quiet office neighbors both try to place a shared decorative paper plant nearer the other as a gift, sliding it back and forth overnight. They finally push their desks into an L shape and set the plant at the shared corner, where its two paper branches point toward both seats.",
  "hook": "It was meant for you.",
  "visible_action": "Plant slides left and right between cuts; two gift tags appear; desks rotate into an L; paper branches open toward both figures.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A gift does not always need a single owner.",
  "gate": "Use a paper plant so its movement makes no unsupported claim about plant behavior.",
  "evidence_class": "fictional_demonstration",
